{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/100915-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-houses-of-the-moon-tribes","id":100915,"title":"Idigam Chronicles Weekly Discussion: Houses of the Moon(Tribes)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-28T15:41:44-07:00","id":100915,"title":"Idigam Chronicles Weekly Discussion: Houses of the Moon(Tribes)","content":"<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/houses-of-the-moon/\" target=\"_blank\">It's not how we hunt, but what we hunt.</a><br /> <br /> That little comment is the biggest distinction betwen the old take on tribes and the new one, and I think it's mostly effective...Sort of. The Hunters and Lords feel a little weird to me, but I can get over that. The main thing I'm curious about is what fulfilling your tribal sacred hunt will do-it's easy to ascribe them as gifts that relate to your prey, but I imagine the entire thing is actually more ritualistic, if freeflowing, than that.<br /> <br /> Also, my love for the Iron Masters has only grown.<br /> <br /> On the whole, I like it. But that's me. As for y'all? Discuss!<br /> <br /> PS: Also, I love the use of the word know in these descriptions. It's very pointed, like when a religious person says &quot;I know [insert beliefs here] are true&quot;-it just invites contestation between wolves of different tribes, but not, necessarily, enough to provoke serious bloodshed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-28-2014, 06:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T15:56:47-07:00","id":100922,"title":"","content":"The Hunters, since you mention them, make sense to me after giving it a little thought. The shartha fit, given the Hosts' tendency to fuck around with loci and mess with the sanctity of the border between Flesh and Shadow.<br /> <br /> I'm having trouble putting words to why the Lords' focus makes sense to me, but it does as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T16:03:36-07:00","id":100927,"title":"","content":"Tribes probably have a Condition, like Agendas in Demon.<br /> <br /> I really like Iron Masters now, I like that concept (I can see a pack hunting in Wall Street). I personally would swap Blood Talons and Storm Lords but that's a personal preference.<br /> <br /> I don't see the arbitrary separation of Shartha mockeries for Hunters in Darkness and the other mockeries that Storm Lords hunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T16:06:17-07:00","id":100928,"title":"","content":"Sharta are &quot;natural&quot; creatures (although, quite obviously, with a World of Darkness twist), neatly fitting the whole nature theme that the Hunters in Darkness have going on.<br /> <br /> If Bone Shadows hunt spirits and Iron Masters hunt men, it makes perfect sense for the Hunters in Darkness to hunt locusts, spiders, rats and the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T16:07:15-07:00","id":100929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amaterasu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/100915-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-houses-of-the-moon-tribes?p=100927#post100927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see the arbitrary separation of Shartha mockeries for Hunters in Darkness and the other mockeries that Storm Lords hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>The shartha are what they are by nature. The other three are matters of active behavior - a magath becomes what it is by incorporating the wrong kind of resonance, the Ridden become what they are by attaching themselves to living things, but a Beshilu is a Beshilu from ratty cradle to ratty grave.<br /> <br /> Assuming the associated Renown categories stay more or less the same, there's a distinct difference between transgression and contamination.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T16:09:13-07:00","id":100931,"title":"","content":"That's what most weirds me out, Amaterasu: I'm not sure why the Hosts deserve distinction from the various Spirit-Possessed(Urged and Ridden), and I'm really not sure why the magath are lumped in with either of them. If anything, the Magath feel like Bone Shadow territory, and the hosts and Spirit-Possessed....well, okay, put that way, it now feels more right, though I couldn't articulate why, but ti still feels like they should be lumped together if not for Satchel's point about the Hosts effect on the Gauntlet(THough isn't that disregarding the snake-hosts, crow-hosts, and the locust host?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T16:11:32-07:00","id":100932,"title":"","content":"Besides the &quot;the Hosts are natural, thus fitting the Hunters in Darkness best&quot; explanation - Black Wolf wants her followers to hunt Sharta. And she'll likely give them powers if they do. What more explanation do you need? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T16:13:38-07:00","id":100934,"title":"","content":"Spirits do what Spirits are, and Spirits are what Spirits do<br /> <br /> So what is it about Black Wolf that makes the Shartha the biggest target in her chosen's rogue's gallery?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Storm Lords got an Update, and it makes some more sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-28-2014, 07:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T16:19:08-07:00","id":100938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/100915-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-houses-of-the-moon-tribes?p=100931#post100931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">still feels like they should be lumped together if not for Satchel's point about the Hosts effect on the Gauntlet(THough isn't that disregarding the snake-hosts, crow-hosts, and the locust host?).</div> </div> </div> </div>The rats and the spiders are the most common Hosts and have those effects, is the thing, and the locusts - who come the closest to seizing the by-the-numbers position of &quot;Third Host&quot; - have a nasty habit of living up to their ancient progenitor's sobriquet of &quot;Famine-Bringer,&quot; and that's going to have negative effects no matter how strong the Zathu is. Meanwhile we don't strictly know <i>what</i> the deal is with the Razilu, and the Crow Host seems uncommon enough, harmless enough, and easily-dealt-with enough that they probably don't ping the radar all that often.<br /> <br /> The defining feature of shartha, though, is that they're fragmentary spirit-as-flesh creatures that get more dangerous the more of themselves they get together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 03-28-2014, 07:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T16:19:42-07:00","id":100939,"title":"","content":"So, I wanted few things changed for the tribes, or simply clarified. A)Why and how werewolves join them, b) make them all different.<br /> <br /> And, this CERTAINLY answers all the questions in a very simple yet clever way, tying it all into being wereWOLVES again. No longer are the tribes mash-ups of the Apocalypse ones that are unclear in their role in Uratha society. Now, each has its own purpose and goal, and tribe has a clear definition.<br /> I like that its tied to the prey, because WtF has so many great foes to use, and it is easy to see werewolves define themselves with the prey they hunt as they are supposed to be replacing Father Wolf. Specialization is helpful.<br /> <br /> For the specific tribes, Blood Talons hunting werewolves makes sense. They are the most martial of the tribes and so would be the most ready TO fight other werewolves. Bone Shadows are almost a given.<br /> <br /> Now, Iron Masters are the most interesting out of the five in my opinion. Instead of being -for- humanity, they are instead against its worse aspects. This changes them from the most human of tribes to the tribe most vary of humans using humanity's own methods to hunt. Clever.<br /> <br /> Hunters hunting those who would hurt the balance makes them the most balance oriented tribe. And Lords hunting the unnatural, well, they are the tribe most likely to go on such a hero quest.<br /> <br /> I can now totally see how tribal gatherings work, as well. The tribe members gather to compare notes, then leave for their packs with the added knowledge.<br /> <br /> All in all, I really like this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T16:20:46-07:00","id":100941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/100915-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-houses-of-the-moon-tribes?p=100929#post100929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The shartha are what they are by nature. The other three are matters of active behavior - a magath becomes what it is by incorporating the wrong kind of resonance, the Ridden become what they are by attaching themselves to living things, but a Beshilu is a Beshilu from ratty cradle to ratty grave.<br /> <br /> Assuming the associated Renown categories stay more or less the same, there's a distinct difference between transgression and contamination.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apparently it was a wrong version. The edited update makes it much better now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T16:21:40-07:00","id":100942,"title":"","content":"Fair enough.<br /> <br /> (man, that vote is like dead even right now)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T16:31:35-07:00","id":100945,"title":"","content":"Urged/Claimed are any random spirits crossing the gauntlet, Shartha are more ancient spirits who can take forms of flesh under specific circumstances. There's a blend from Bone Shadows hunting things in/of the Shadow, to the Hunters in Darkness with the Hosts, to the Storm Lords hunting the possessed, to the Iron Masters hunting humanity. About the only one that can be blended together easily in that manner is Blood Talons hunting Uratha.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T16:33:59-07:00","id":100947,"title":"","content":"Well, at least there's not a lot of fighting over grey areas.<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, fuck, this is your department. Have fun, and don't let it bite you-it's leaking battery acid.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T16:37:19-07:00","id":100948,"title":"","content":"Yes. I can see a pack with each of the tribes represented working well together. Or not, because they can't prioritize.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T16:52:20-07:00","id":100960,"title":"","content":"Blargh! You beat me to making this thread all because I was busy doing something unproductive when the post came out<br /> <br /> On topic however, I really like the fact that each tribe has a distinct section they deal with and now gives players a roleplay incentive for selecting of tribe rather than simply trying to choose whichever fit your renown of choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":444,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","user":"Dessembrae","date":". 03-28-2014, 08:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T17:27:25-07:00","id":100986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/100915-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-houses-of-the-moon-tribes?p=100960#post100960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blargh! You beat me to making this thread all because I was busy doing something unproductive when the post came out<br /> <br /> On topic however, I really like the fact that each tribe has a distinct section they deal with and now gives players a roleplay incentive for selecting of tribe rather than simply trying to choose whichever fit your renown of choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hahahahaha! Self-destructive negligence of duties wins again!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T17:43:16-07:00","id":100993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/100915-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-houses-of-the-moon-tribes?p=100986#post100986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hahahahaha! Self-destructive negligence of duties wins again!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm on vacation next Friday...the war is on!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T20:32:22-07:00","id":101054,"title":"","content":"Storm Lords get Ridden?<br /> <br /> Makes...perfect sense, actually. Claimed are the children of spirit and flesh melding in the worst possible way, and thus it is the most akin to the role of Father Wolf as keeper of the balance.<br /> <br /> Besides, the Ridden's primary trait is unpredictability. That usually requires some degree of coordination and planning to counter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T20:52:33-07:00","id":101057,"title":"","content":"Hmm....Actually, I think that unpredictability is better countered by adaptability, since unpredictability exists to trump planning. Totally right on Coordination though.<br /> <br /> As for the ones most akin to Father Wolf...I don't know about that. First off, all the first born are kin to Urfarah, which means they all bear some of his spiritual identity. Each one probably thinks they are they closest.<br /> <br /> Bickering of elder gods asides, the Storm Lords may be the closest to the parental side of Urfarah, or at least to his side as the lead of the pack, but balance keepers they were not before. THat was more the Hunters. In fact, put that way, it almost makes more sense to flip the two due to the idea of legacy...if there still wasn't some kind of damnedable hidden thematic that feels right for the Storm Lords over the possessed.<br /> <br /> Maybe it comes to that point-I don't remember where it was written-where the Iminir generally displayed powers of dominance over people or dominance over the elements. THe Natural world and it's people(Which include The People) are the Storm Lords to guide, watch, and protect, and like hell an unholy hybrid of the two is going to get away with ignoring that. Or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T21:52:31-07:00","id":101073,"title":"","content":"Well, I gotta say, I like this approuch to the Tribes. However, I'm of the opinion that the Blood Talon and Storm Lord &quot;chosen prey&quot; should be switched. It makes sense to me that Storm Lords should hunt other Werewolves to prove their alpha status. While Blood Talons should hunt the Ridden to prove thier martial skills. I don't know. That's how I see things.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That being said, I think inter-Tribal packs are going to be more interesting to run than they were before. I can't wait.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T22:01:06-07:00","id":101081,"title":"","content":"You know, one thing I just realized, that I kind of love, is that the Blood Talons clearly hunt werewolves. Not only does it flat out say that, it clarifies by saying they mostly hunt the Pure, but not just them.<br /> <br /> <i>All the other tribes are werewolves</i>.<br /> <br /> Why I like this is that it both feels like a fulfillment and subversion of the classic warrior class thing. On the one hand, throughout history, leaders of armies have usurped the conventional ruler and used their might to subjugate a populace, and with an advantage against werewolves, the Blood Talons, who were the classic fighter/warrior tribe before, can now do this, and it's a subtle threat in any interaction with them-declaring yourself a Blood Talon comes with the unsaid promise of &quot;I can fuck you up if I want to&quot;. On the other hand, werewolves are <i>not</i> the average citizen populace, nor is any alpha like most emperors or kings of humanity-each and everyone of them has the unstated promise of &quot;You can fuck me up, but I can and will make you take the mileage for it&quot;.<br /> <br /> It's kinda cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T22:02:50-07:00","id":101082,"title":"","content":"I'm a little disappointed that the Tribes aren't really cultural groups (I don't want spins on human cultures like in WtA, but I'd hoped for more heritage identity/customs/etc), but this is way better than previous canon where the Tribes kind of come off as just secondary Auspices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T22:10:06-07:00","id":101085,"title":"","content":"I'd say hold off on that assessment. Human cultures are informed by the elements of their environment,including what they hunt-contrast native Americas with their buffaloes and bobcats and India with their elephants and tigers. The contrast that with African tribes with their elephants and Siberian tribes with their tigers. What we hunt shapes our culture as much as the way our rivers, our fields and deserts, and the rest of our environments do.<br /> <br /> It doesn't take much how the Blood Talons we knew became the way they are by focusing on werewolves, nor Iron Masters with Humanity or the Bone Shadows with Spirits. Their chosen prey reflects on them pretty easily. The culture, I assume, is still there, it's just now more sharply defined by a root idea-an idea that, by the way, is radically different from human sources(or at least more alien). As an example, I don't think many cultures have kept hunting as such a central position to their culture as the Uratha have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-29-2014, 01:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T01:54:13-07:00","id":101147,"title":"","content":"Things to note in new world vs old:<br /> <br /> Apocalypse features Tribes based on cultural identities and ideologies. Spirits operate much differently in Apocalypse (lore wise not mechanics)<br /> <br /> Forsaken features Tribes that appear to be grouped more on how their spirit responds. They are creatures of spirit and should be driven to certain things like most spirits (Idigam aside).<br /> <br /> I always liked that Forsakens tribes were ideological over cultural. That way we don't have a whole pack of say... almost nazi werewolves in the first edition.<br /> <br /> And oi! Blood Talons damn well deserve to take it to the pure! They train their bodies from the beggining to be weapons. They are (or were) the combined ideas of the Wendigo and Fenrir without the racial bias. Not to say they aren't capable of differing activities, but Tribes of the Moon makes it pretty clear they're a &quot;screw this shit, we're hitting it hard first&quot; Tribe, and what else pushes the limits of physical combat and wits besides another uratha?<br /> <br /> The Tribes all fit very well when ya think about it. The Storm Lords hunting other uratha as their alpha status? Nein, I'd say it makes more sense to lead by <i>example</i>. And so we have the &quot;Alpha&quot; tribe performing Urfahra's duties in the physical, while the Bone Shadows perform a similar hunt in the Hisil. The Storm Lords are still in the position to lead, and with the urged and claimed priorities, probably the best at dealing with incursions in the territory from such threats. They're the ones with the eyes on the prize as it were. Blood Talons are just out to kick ass and take renown.<br /> <br /> Edit: I previously thought of the Iron folk as being something similar to Glass walkers, and wanted nothing to do with them. This new motif of theirs makes them sound almost sexy as player characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T02:24:00-07:00","id":101160,"title":"","content":"Well, I guess with the new focus of Storm Lords on the Claimed, Idigam chronicle might use a revision or reprint of those too. As well as more examples of Azlu/Beshilu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T05:19:33-07:00","id":101209,"title":"","content":"If the main antagonists of my game are, say, the Pure, does that mean characters who aren't Blood Talons will be substantially less effective?<br /> (And the same applies to other tribe/prey combinations).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T05:38:56-07:00","id":101216,"title":"","content":"It seems more like the situation where the ST should tailor the antagonists to the PCs. If you're a group made up mostly of Blood Talons the enemy should primarily be other werewolves, but that doesn't mean you don't deal with spirits/spirit-claimed/shartha/humanity/whatnot. Its just that by slapping your Tribe down on the sheet it says to the ST this is what my character favors for their hunting. <br /> <br /> I figure it'll work similarly to how Agendas work in Demon. You gain Beats for dealing with your Tribal Prey, and resolving it nets you neat bonuses to finish the deal. Think of it more as an incentive for favoring something rather than a detriment.<br /> <br /> Besides, I doubt your powers stop working because the enemy isn't the one you normally like to chew on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T05:41:23-07:00","id":101217,"title":"","content":"I didn't have any problem with Storm Lords having the Claimed/Urged as prey for different reasons, but after you guys mentioned it, it does make sense for the Alphas to lead by example and do what Urfarah was suposed to do.<br /> <br /> Idigam Chronicles is building up to be one of my favourite games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T05:54:23-07:00","id":101221,"title":"","content":"What I feel is an important point that is being missed right now is even though the Storm Lords deal with things such as Claimed, it isn't their only goal in life. While it gives them the primary direction, who's to say that they can't be the alphas and the leaders we are used to? I actually like the fact that the Claimed are a high target for them since they make some of the most complex and difficult characters to deal with due to their human/spirit nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T06:26:12-07:00","id":101227,"title":"","content":"I... don't like. I'm actually rather opposed to this. By what you hunt? So, if my plot revolves around Sharatha or the Pure, I'm going to get my players to heavily lean towards one Tribe? <br /> <br /> My gut reaction is to be opposed to the whole &quot;by what you hunt&quot; thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T06:39:53-07:00","id":101234,"title":"","content":"Not necesarily. Nothing says that:<br /> <br /> a) Those are the only prey each Tribe are after and...<br /> b) ...other Tribes are less equiped to deal with prey outside its primary focus.<br /> <br /> If anything this way of presenting Tribes allows for multiple Tribe packs (wich I think were the default) to make a lot of sense, while the idea of single-Tribe packs is at the very least as posible as before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T06:42:07-07:00","id":101235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/100915-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-houses-of-the-moon-tribes?p=101227#post101227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I... don't like. I'm actually rather opposed to this. By what you hunt? So, if my plot revolves around Sharatha or the Pure, I'm going to get my players to heavily lean towards one Tribe? My gut reaction is to be opposed to the whole &amp;quot;by what you hunt&amp;quot; thing.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not necessarily. It's not like non-blood talons are inept at fighting the pure, or blood talons are bad at hunting things other than the pure. It just gives them focus. Their tribal culture centers around fighting other werewolves, that's all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T06:51:42-07:00","id":101237,"title":"","content":"Also, note that there's a good deal of overlap between prey categories.<br /> <br /> Now I wonder if the Pure Tribes will be also defined by their prey of choice or by other thing. I could see the Ivory Claws hunting ghosts and other undead due to the tribal ban, for example. Not so sure about Fire Touched and Predator Kings, the last would probably hunt <i>everything</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T06:52:52-07:00","id":101238,"title":"","content":"Not a fan of it either. It seems oversimplified and tacked on and specializing the Tribes even further. Pack trumping the other social groups? Hell yeah, always went by that. But a singular prey tribal focus... that's what the big hub-bub was about? Really? I'm not the only one finding it a bit contrived in a poor way at the moment it seems from who I've talked to. I don't mind preferred prey, I've tinkered with that notion in the past regarding what spirits get consistently targetted and relevant to a tribe, but this seems quite a lot more focused than even that.<br /> <br /> I'm assuming (and I hate assuming) that there's quite a bit more to it; the spoilers have been very thin on information beyond the root idea behind them. They're obviously not the full scoop, so lacking the additional context via more &quot;meat&quot; they could turn out to be even better. But going by what I have seen? Harmony revision has quite a bit of potential once we know more (though the lack of Breaking Point spoilers kinda makes the rest kinda thin), but so far, I'm liking that sliding scale idea.<br /> <br /> The Tribal prey focus? My gut knee-jerk reaction says &quot;If I wanted to play a series of H:tV Compacts with shapeshifting powers, I'd whip out Spirit Slayers and get tinkering&quot;.<br /> <br /> Not a fan. Perhaps that will change when we see more to do with it, but this one is a 2 steps forwards, 3 steps back spoiler for me as presented. Way too particular, focused and fiddly given the baggage it brings in, and I'm getting that creeping dread of the DnD borrowed aspects W:tA was riddled with early on creeping right back into Forsaken all over again.<br /> <br /> I was hoping for more on Tribal interactions, the relevance of the Pure to it, treatments on how prey tweaks a tribe and its outlooks, possibly werewolf origin stories as related to tribe, something with more content to it.I got an overblown hunting specialization.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":114,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","user":"Tatterdemalion King","date":".  poor grammar less poor 03-29-2014, 09:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T07:10:42-07:00","id":101244,"title":"","content":"We're right back to &quot;Proper tool for the job&quot; and &quot;the right Tribe/Auspice/Renown mix&quot; all over again until we see this clarified, something that was a severe pain in the ass previously. The game is building your character for you in a soft (or hard) way.<br /> <br /> It's a step away from the &quot;we need a rogue, a bard, a wizard, a warrior, and a paladin&quot; rut Auspices were saddled with since their inception, but narrowing down a Tribe and presenting a very particular specialization and focus as the Big Thing tm is... well, it's just digging another rut in that area instead.<br /> <br /> Unless there's a further fundamental shift to the notion of Tribes (and how one joins one), I can't get behind this yet. I should comfortably be able to make a Hunter in Darkness who tangles with other Werewolves and doesn't feel like he's getting shortchanged for doing it and not being a Blood Talon. You know, like when you played a Tribe member who's Renown wasn't &quot;optomized&quot; and &quot;encouraged&quot; to be made a particular way not to get stiffed previously.<br /> <br /> This half-spoiler isn't exactly helping that; we're just getting a bunch of player assumptions without the content to back it on both ends. That's not too helpful. Hopefully we'll see more to do this so we can make a better assessment one way or the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T07:12:15-07:00","id":101246,"title":"","content":"Let me clarify. Most of the time when I come up with a werewolf story, it often includes some kind of antagonist. Someone to threaten the pact's territory. I feel like, when I decide on the chronicle's Big Bad, I'm deciding that &quot;this game is going to be Blood Talon focused.&quot; Or &quot;this game is Iron Master focused.&quot; Hells. Idigam. The titular beings of the new edition. That's a Bone Shadow focused game now.<br /> <br /> It feels like its just that much harder to have a non-Tribe focused game now. Its pretty easy to pull off in Vampire, or Mage. I'm a bit harder pressed in Werewolf now. <br /> <br /> And I really, really don't like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-29-2014, 10:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T07:29:12-07:00","id":101253,"title":"","content":"Actually Idigam have been explicitely stated as being an out of context problem for every Tribe, so... no, not really.<br /> <br /> As for it being more difficult than in other games, we just don't know yet. You are maybe taking it a bit monolithic, like: &quot;this is the only thing we hunt and the only ones which can hunt it properly&quot; wich again no, not really.<br /> <br /> Does each Tribe now have a clear focus in case you want to base a chronicle or story around it if you want to focus on the themes of a particular Tribe? Yes. Does it mean I can only play certain Tribes if I include certain antagonists? Not at all.<br /> It happens the same with vampire Clans, if I want a chronicle around the corruption of power I can do it with any clan, but Ventrue are better for it; if I want one focusing on the isolation brought up by the Curse, it can be played with any Clan, but Nosferatu probably do it better, same with the ravagings of the Beast and Gangrel, the seductive aspects of being a vampire an Daeva, etc, etc.<br /> <br /> Mage actually is worse for that, giving the specialization of the Arcana. Werewolf doesn't have that problem as the tools needed for engaging any of the listed prey are possesed by all werewolves.<br /> <br /> EDIT: and I believe I should stop posting. I don't wanna come out as trying to shut anyone down. People disagreeing with changes is good, is what makes things improved. I'm not trying to make you like what you don't like, just pointing out that you may be comming to conclussions based on false asumptions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 03-29-2014, 10:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T08:34:07-07:00","id":101284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/100915-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-houses-of-the-moon-tribes?p=101253#post101253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually Idigam have been explicitely stated as being an out of context problem for every Tribe, so... no, not really.</div> </div> </div> </div> I have not seen that said.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for it being more difficult than in other games, we just don't know yet. You are maybe taking it a bit monolithic, like: &quot;this is the only thing we hunt and the only ones which can hunt it properly&quot; wich again no, not really. </div> </div> </div> No, that's just you reading something I didn't say. What I did say was this:<br /> <br /> I sit down with my players and tell them &quot;The main opponents are Pure, and this is the theme of the game.&quot; They're going to naturally lean to Blood Talons. Pure stories are now defined as &quot;Blood Talon stories.&quot; You can play other things. I never once said otherwise - that's just people who want to read things into what I said, but never intended.<br /> <br /> But, based on what the article seems to be saying, it IS going to be a BT focused chronicle. That's an issue. That's my problem. Its creating a bias on what y-axis you pick. It shouldn't be. I can run a strix,VII, evil Prince, rogue ghoul, or similiar story and it be clan/cov independant. In Mage, it'd be Seer, Banisher, Tremere, Scelesti, Acamoth (ala Prince of 1000 Leaves). I can't say the same about Werewolf now, and that isn't something I care for.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> EDIT: and I believe I should stop posting. I don't wanna come out as trying to shut anyone down. People disagreeing with changes is good, is what makes things improved. I'm not trying to make you like what you don't like, just pointing out that you may be comming to conclussions based on false asumptions. </div> </div> </div> Which is why I'm saying things like &quot;my gut reaction?&quot; No offense, but it seems that you, and a few others here, are coming to false conclusions about what I say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-29-2014, 11:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T08:44:50-07:00","id":101292,"title":"","content":"I dislike what I've seen so far; for the same reasons as MCN.<br /> <br /> We still need more information though; and as thus, it's hard to judge the quality of the new tribes. I'm particularly interested in how to use the tribes in the context of a story - for example, is it possible to run a story in which antagonist X is to feature prominently, and none of the PCs are part of the corresponding tribe? This topic needs to be covered in the book (and I'm confident that it will be).<br /> <br /> (and, respectfully, I'm not interested in an answer to this question that isn't from someone who's working on the book.)<br /> <br /> I hope that the storytelling chapter of the book is up to the usual high standards of quality (these chapters are usually the best parts of the corebooks).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":286,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","user":"Christian A","date":". 03-29-2014, 11:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T08:45:37-07:00","id":101294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tatterdemalion King</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tribal prey focus? My gut knee-jerk reaction says &quot;If I wanted to play a series of H:tV Compacts with shapeshifting powers, I'd whip out Spirit Slayers and get tinkering&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Coincidentally, my knee-jerk reaction to your &quot;Forsaken Overhaul&quot; was &quot;If I wanted to play shapeshifter vampires I'd make a gangrel with B&amp;S.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tatterdemalion King</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should comfortably be able to make a Hunter in Darkness who tangles with other Werewolves and doesn't feel like he's getting shortchanged for doing it and not being a Blood Talon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Make yourself a Lodge for that purpose.<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> I think it's a fallacy to think that &quot;because my tribe's chosen prey isn't X it means I SUCK at hunting X.&quot; - Look at how we hunt as a sport. We look for challenges. Any Uratha who succeeds, on his own or barely, in a hunt to something which isn't his favored prey should be recognized for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T09:03:50-07:00","id":101304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/100915-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-houses-of-the-moon-tribes?p=101294#post101294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's a fallacy to think that &quot;because my tribe's chosen prey isn't X it means I SUCK at hunting X.&quot; - Look at how we hunt as a sport. We look for challenges. Any Uratha who succeeds, on his own or barely, in a hunt to something which isn't his favored prey should be recognized for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree! There's also the fact that the entire existence of the Idigam - the out-of-context problem, as it has often been stated - demonstrates quite well that it's interesting and thematic to introduce enemies to the game that the protagonists might not be prepared to handle. The game should absolutely support throwing a bunch of spirits at a pack of Iron Masters who're not well prepared to deal with spirits, narratively and thematically. The Forsaken are hunted by many things. Specialisation helps, but it can and should also be a liability.<br /> <br /> I think it's fairly likely that members of tribes will get some sort of advantage/benefit/incentive to hunting their selected prey. What I *don't* want to see is this advantage/benefit/incentive being seen as an absolute *necessity* when hunting prey X. As MCN implied, I don't want players to think &quot;oh! Chris put on his storyteller hat and told us that this game will have lots of Pure! So we should all play Blood Talons!&quot;. From what we know (which, as I said, really isn't much), the current tribe setup might encourage that sort of thinking, and I believe that might be a little problematic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":286,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","user":"Christian A","date":". 03-29-2014, 12:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T09:10:00-07:00","id":101312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/100915-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-houses-of-the-moon-tribes?p=101294#post101294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Coincidentally, my knee-jerk reaction to your &quot;Forsaken Overhaul&quot; was &quot;If I wanted to play shapeshifter vampires I'd make a gangrel with B&amp;S.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Make yourself a Lodge for that purpose.<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> I think it's a fallacy to think that &quot;because my tribe's chosen prey isn't X it means I SUCK at hunting X.&quot; - Look at how we hunt as a sport. We look for challenges. Any Uratha who succeeds, on his own or barely, in a hunt to something which isn't his favored prey should be recognized for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The former has no relevance to this conversation save as a jab; the overhaul for my long-running Chronicle has absolutely -no- bearing on this, especially when it has been tailored for my player's and game needs. Why even bring it up?<br /> <br /> Did I say you'd suck? Nope. Neither did MCN. I referenced being shortchanged; it seems a very, very odd notion in my eye that a core facet of their society makes you better against one particular form of prey, and if you don't play that Tribe, you're not going to have as much efficiency hunting something as a werewolf. That's why Vigil comes to mind; Compacts with particular supernaturals they focus on that define them. With the information we have currently it -heavily- reminds me of that. It's &quot;My Tribe is the tools for the Job. Tribe X is a bow for that prey. Tribe Y is the punt gun for that. Tribe Z has the snare.&quot; That really doesn't jive with me.<br /> <br /> We've not seen Lodges, or any changes to them yet. That's a pretty bold statement to make without any information to work from regarding what they now do, and how they're now structured.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T09:39:12-07:00","id":101334,"title":"","content":"I don't want to get too far into spoilers that are rightfully Stew's, but I wanted to clarify this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/100915-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-houses-of-the-moon-tribes?p=101292#post101292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We still need more information though; and as thus, it's hard to judge the quality of the new tribes. I'm particularly interested in how to use the tribes in the context of a story - for example, is it possible to run a story in which antagonist X is to feature prominently, and none of the PCs are part of the corresponding tribe?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, any pack can hunt any prey. Tribal prey represent a cultural focus with some mechanical teeth, but you don't need a specialist from a certain tribe to take down certain prey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T09:41:16-07:00","id":101335,"title":"","content":"That's good to read; thanks, Rose!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T09:42:13-07:00","id":101338,"title":"","content":"I mentioned earlier how the animals a group hunts informs their culture in an earlier post. I'm gonna build on that in two ways.<br /> <br /> 1)While there are huge differences between killing a bear and killing a snake(namely I shouldn't even call hunting a snake hunting really), consider that learning how to hunt an elk informs how to hunt many other animals, even if it's not a usual translation. The skills of one may not perfectly apply all the time, but it's easier for someone with expertise with one type of prey to adapt and apply that to others.<br /> <br /> Let's apply this idea to the Tribes....Because it's even simpler to see. For example, let's go with the Storm Lords and their targets of the Spirit-Possessed. Quite frankly, while the specialization helps, consider that a Spirit Ridden often has similar(if sometimes diminished) advantages as a werewolf, as a creature of flesh and spirit with the two warping each other, so a Iminir isn't going to be freaking lost filling in for the Blood Talon. The Shartha also apply to the moniker, albeit with a tough escape mechanism that unless you spend a lot of time thinking on isn't going to be easy to deal with, but by all means a Lord is going to be able to handle the stuffed flesh bags in their first incarnation thanks to what they know about the Spirit Ridden just as easily. To deal with them either as Urged or as Ridden, You have to understand the way a spirit and a human thinks and how they respond under different circumstances in order to harry,trap and deal with them, so while their knowledge isn't as extensive as the Bone Shadows or the Iron Masters, they have a fair amount of knowledge under their belt because they needed some of this knowledge when hunting their chosen prey.<br /> <br /> Other tribes might not have so lucky a spread(In fact, I suspect now that the reason the Lords specialized in the Spirit Possessed is because it does give them so much of broad advantage), but the simple fact is that it's kind of stupid to assume that just because your Tribe claims that <i>this</i> is the biggest prey means you'll be left on the sidelines when <i>this</i> isn't the main focus. It's not hard to jury rig what you know into application for whatever the circumstance is.<br /> <br /> 2)The chosen prey thing is foundational. It is the seed, not the tree. It's a cornerstone, not the house. The Tribe is not the Prey, the Prey is the Tribe.<br /> <br /> Again, I already brought up the idea of how the things we hunt informs culture-but it is very important to understand that it i<i>nforms </i>it, rather than completely <i>define</i> it. Will it matter more with the Uratha, with their focus on Hunting, tradition, etc., etc.? Sure, yeah. But it's not going to be all consuming.<br /> <br /> So with that said, a few other things.<br /> <br /> @MCN: If I was your player, and you told me you were running a a game with the Pure as the main antagonist, I'd probably play an Iron Master, maybe a Storm Lord.<br /> <br /> Why? <i>Because I like playing Iron Masters and Storm Lords</i>.<br /> <br /> I understand people's concerns about twinkery, but quite frankly WoD has never struck me as a game that's rewarding when you twink-it lives more off of the characters being characters that optimally primed to take things out like a nuke. If a person twinks their character to be a supreme Werewolf Killer, that's fine, that's a concept in and of itself, and so long as it works as a character that's cool, but I don't think WoD plays out like that most of the time.<br /> <br /> I think there's a problem in the way we conceive of our stories. I build my stories off of the characters, so that might just be me, but even when I come up with generic ideas, it's never really a &quot;this is my big antagonist, this game is defined by that&quot;. For generic scenarios, I build off of a theme and flesh out the city and characters, including the antagonists, from there. I have trouble coming up with a scenario that is explicitly &quot;This is a Pure Driven game, ergo a Blood Talon game&quot;. I tend to think more in terms of &quot;This is a game about familial expectations&quot; and build from there, and if the final antagonist is a Pure who happens to magically be everyone's grandfather, that's circumstantial. Probably the one to strike him down is not the Blood Talon, but whoever is hurt by him the most.<br /> <br /> I'm just saying, maybe we want to step back from the strokes and see the painting.<br /> <br /> Annnd I actually don't have as much to say as I thought I did.<br /> <br /> EDIT: The more is revealed about the Storm Lords, the more they make sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-29-2014, 12:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T09:56:51-07:00","id":101341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/100915-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-houses-of-the-moon-tribes?p=101334#post101334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't want to get too far into spoilers that are rightfully Stew's, but I wanted to clarify this.<br /> Yes, any pack can hunt any prey. Tribal prey represent a cultural focus with some mechanical teeth, but you don't need a specialist from a certain tribe to take down certain prey.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks Rose!<br /> <br /> The way I am choosing to look at this is each Tribe has a specific/cultural long term focus and as such, have a certain mechanical bonus for hunting that type of prey. This in no way means other tribes can't hunt them or even develop a bias versus a type of prey they are not typically known for. It is much the way that Auspices work in that Ithaeur have an advantage with rituals due to the auspice blessing, but that doesn't mean you can't find a Rahu ritualist who is just as good.<br /> <br /> Now admittedly, the mechanical benefits are still unknown, but I doubt it would be something earthshatteringly overpowered compared to the rest such as Blood Talons deal aggravated damage to werewolves while everyone else does lethal. It may be something as simple as +1 extra die to resist werewolf powers or +1 to use powers against them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T10:21:03-07:00","id":101349,"title":"","content":"Actually... maybe you <b>are</b> the bane of your chosen prey by virtue of it being your chosen prey. Or that could be incorporated in some manner of Gift.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T10:33:19-07:00","id":101358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/100915-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-houses-of-the-moon-tribes?p=101349#post101349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually... maybe you <b>are</b> the bane of your chosen prey by virtue of it being your chosen prey. Or that could be incorporated in some manner of Gift.</div> </div> </div> </div>while I couldn't completely discount that as a possibility, it sounds extremely strong in context of the nWoD system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T10:38:56-07:00","id":101360,"title":"","content":"So blood talons cause aggro damage just by touching uratha? I'm down!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T10:41:06-07:00","id":101361,"title":"","content":"I'll have to read up on Rank again in GMC, but that sounds more like a Predator King thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T10:44:42-07:00","id":101363,"title":"","content":"At best I can imagine those as very high-level Gifts, if they exist at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T10:47:17-07:00","id":101365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/100915-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-houses-of-the-moon-tribes?p=101360#post101360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So blood talons cause aggro damage just by touching uratha? I'm down!</div> </div> </div> </div>So that's how internet facts get started.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T10:48:16-07:00","id":101366,"title":"","content":"Absolutely. After all, you read it on the internet!<br /> <br /> That joke's probably not as funny as I think it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T10:54:47-07:00","id":101371,"title":"","content":"I'm very interested in what sort of powers/mechanical incentive the Iron Masters get for &quot;hunting people&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T10:57:48-07:00","id":101376,"title":"","content":"I wonder to what degree the OTHER aspects of the Tribes will still be in-tact. Are Hunters in Darkness still especially concerned with preserving natural places and connecting with their wolf side? Are Storm Lords still the self-assumed leaders of the Uratha? Do Bone Shadows still have a special association with death and the underworld?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T10:58:46-07:00","id":101377,"title":"","content":"I wonder if the Pure Tribes have some new question that defines them each as tribes as well... I doubt the &quot;hunt&quot; question works for them, unless they've been unrecognizably overhauled, as it'd be redundant with the Predator Kings hunting humanity and uratha as their &quot;niche&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T10:59:46-07:00","id":101379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/houses-of-the-moon/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/houses-of-the-moon/\" target=\"_blank\"> Houses of the Moon &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/houses-of-the-moon/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/houses-of-the-moon/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> gonna post the link to the blog post as Stew is actively answering questions there. I believe a lot of the concerns are being answered there, thanks Stew!<br /> <br /> From what it's looking like, it sort of reminds me of the structure of Apocalypse packs, but instead of auspice its the tribe. So you have differing leaders depending on the situation. It actually gives multiple players a chance to shine, assuming the ST knows what they're doing (things can get a bit hellish at times with organization... or if you have a player who decides he wants to rob a guess store for pants).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T11:00:26-07:00","id":101380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/100915-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-houses-of-the-moon-tribes?p=101376#post101376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder to what degree the OTHER aspects of the Tribes will still be in-tact. Are Hunters in Darkness still especially concerned with preserving natural places and connecting with their wolf side? Are Storm Lords still the self-assumed leaders of the Uratha? Do Bone Shadows still have a special association with death and the underworld?</div> </div> </div> </div>To quote Stew, &quot;The hunt is part of an explanation for why the tribes are the way they are, not a complete replacement. It\u2019s an addition and a refocus, not a complete rewrite.&quot;<br /> <br /> I guess the answer to your questions is &quot;yes&quot;, yes. I'll be happy if it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T11:01:32-07:00","id":101382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/100915-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-houses-of-the-moon-tribes?p=101377#post101377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if the Pure Tribes have some new question that defines them each as tribes as well... I doubt the &quot;hunt&quot; question works for them, unless they've been unrecognizably overhauled, as it'd be redundant with the Predator Kings hunting humanity and uratha as their &quot;niche&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div> I would assume that they all hunt werewolves (the Forsaken, to be specific) just as the Blood Talons, with them taking the thematic role of providing the other side of the Werewolf experience and all \u2013 but hey, I\u2019m sure they've come up with something cool.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T11:05:14-07:00","id":101383,"title":"","content":"I wonder if we could see an interplay of auspice and tribes.<br /> what if being a blood talon gave you a +2 against other werewolves but to what exactly it would apply is dependent on auspice.<br /> The Rahu would get it in a straight fight<br /> Ithaeur to craft fetis damaging werewolves or rituals that impede werewolves<br /> Irakka to scout a lair of known werewolves.<br /> <br /> Well you get the gist.<br /> I think that could be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T11:05:55-07:00","id":101384,"title":"","content":".....what do Bale Hounds hunt...?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T11:06:57-07:00","id":101385,"title":"","content":"(if I had to guess, I'd say the Fire-Touched hunt unbelievers/heretics [the Forsaken], the Ivory Claws hunt the impure [the Forsaken] and the Predator Kings hunt predators [the Forsaken]).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T11:08:28-07:00","id":101386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/100915-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-houses-of-the-moon-tribes?p=101382#post101382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I would assume that they all hunt werewolves (the Forsaken, to be specific) just as the Blood Talons, with them taking the thematic role of providing the other side of the Werewolf experience and all \u2013 but hey, I\u2019m sure they've come up with something cool.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I saw Stew said they are a completely different matter entirely. So they're not defined by what they hunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T11:10:03-07:00","id":101387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/100915-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-houses-of-the-moon-tribes?p=101384#post101384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.....what do Bale Hounds hunt...?</div> </div> </div> </div>Things and people of purity (not in the Anshega sense). Lunes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T11:11:09-07:00","id":101388,"title":"","content":"The Pure are more inclined to have a predators paradise ya?<br /> <br /> I'd argue that the Predator Kings are more about annihilating humanity. Absolutely and completely. Different from the Iron folk as I imagine them to be hunting rapists and murderers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T11:11:31-07:00","id":101389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/100915-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-houses-of-the-moon-tribes?p=101386#post101386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So they're not defined by what they hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a plausible interpretation of &quot;the pure tribes are\u2026 a different matter&quot;, but not the only one. The defining feature of werewolves is that they hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T11:11:54-07:00","id":101390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/100915-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-houses-of-the-moon-tribes?p=101384#post101384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.....what do Bale Hounds hunt...?</div> </div> </div> </div>Virtue, and happiness, everywhere. Soulless Wolf ate the spiritual reflection of Santa Claus already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T11:16:34-07:00","id":101393,"title":"","content":"All hail Virruk-Ur!!! er... I mean... dammit Santa? All those poor children... so much sorrow everywhere!!!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T11:23:12-07:00","id":101396,"title":"","content":"I like that the Tribes have something concrete to do, and these Hunting themes seem like a good way to bringing it all together.<br /> <br /> I kinda wish that these previews wouldn't give a one-dimensional summary of the Tribes (only focussing on what they Hunt seems to present the idea that this is now the Tribal identity), it would help better.<br /> <br /> Regarding the &quot;Pure problem = Blood Talon problem&quot; point, I can imagine the spirit allies will cause enough headache of the resident Bone Shadow to have fun with, and the human allies (of the Ivory Claw for example) to entertain the Iron Master. Most antagonists wouldn't be working solely in isolation (or at least, I don't think I would).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/417-the_duck","name":"the_duck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T11:37:12-07:00","id":101400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>the_duck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/100915-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-houses-of-the-moon-tribes?p=101396#post101396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kinda wish that these previews wouldn't give a one-dimensional summary of the Tribes (only focussing on what they Hunt seems to present the idea that this is now the Tribal identity), it would help better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Much as with <i>Blood and Smoke</i>, it's only practical for us to address pieces of the game in each post. The rest of the setting is definitely still there. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 03-29-2014, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T12:24:01-07:00","id":101420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/100915-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-houses-of-the-moon-tribes?p=101388#post101388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Pure are more inclined to have a predators paradise ya? I'd argue that the Predator Kings are more about annihilating humanity. Absolutely and completely. Different from the Iron folk as I imagine them to be hunting rapists and murderers.</div> </div> </div> </div> From the blog post, I don't think the Iron Masters hunt individuals. They hunt institutions, groups, organizations. They'd be less interested in that one rapist and more interested in the underground sex trade ring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T12:24:23-07:00","id":101421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/100915-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-houses-of-the-moon-tribes?p=101400#post101400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Much as with <i>Blood and Smoke</i>, it's only practical for us to address pieces of the game in each post. The rest of the setting is definitely still there. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I know, that sentence went through many drafts. I'm aware there are constraints (damn them! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ), and I know we can't have everything (in fact we're lucky to have anything). I makes me look forward to the eventual release!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/417-the_duck","name":"the_duck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T21:37:27-07:00","id":101742,"title":"","content":"Suppose that makes sense. I was thinking on a more local scale. A guy raping lots of women on a college campus would attract their attention neh? And with multi tribal packs theres always that &quot;alone time&quot; that they might need to make sure they don't gank each other. Assuming Kuruth works the same way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T23:09:07-07:00","id":101776,"title":"","content":"Don't forget Iron Masters 'honor their territory in all things'. A human predator (rapist/murderer/something else) targeting victims in a location that changes the energies of the place and attracts more negative spirits is going to get a lot more attention from an Iron Master than one whose actions don't negatively affect the territory.<br /> <br /> And since Stew offered Harmony or Kuruth as the first decision point of his development blog, it's fair to assume he has something to share about Kuruth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T00:04:50-07:00","id":101795,"title":"","content":"Oh, sure. I didn't mean to imply they <i>don't</i> hunt individuals. It's just not really their focus. I mean, if some serial rapist is messing up the spirit mojo all over the pack's territory on the college campus... Wouldn't <i>any</i> Uratha want to put a stop to that, regardless of Tribe? It's examples like this that showcase why the tribal focus on a type of prey is clearly more about informing their culture than being The Thing They Exist To Fight. All Uratha are obviously going to hunt all of the given prey types, its just a matter of what they as a group believe to be the most dangerous threat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T00:08:44-07:00","id":101796,"title":"","content":"Agreed. Every tribe would fight such a predator if they had time. Iron Masters, and Hunters in Darkness if the attacks occurred on a sacred place within the territory, would *make time*.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T08:19:06-07:00","id":101940,"title":"","content":"Probably we will see new gift lists for tribes , to reflect their prey focus .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2194-furry","name":"Furry","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T08:54:52-07:00","id":101955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/100915-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-houses-of-the-moon-tribes?p=101795#post101795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, sure. I didn't mean to imply they <i>don't</i> hunt individuals. It's just not really their focus. I mean, if some serial rapist is messing up the spirit mojo all over the pack's territory on the college campus... Wouldn't <i>any</i> Uratha want to put a stop to that, regardless of Tribe? It's examples like this that showcase why the tribal focus on a type of prey is clearly more about informing their culture than being The Thing They Exist To Fight. All Uratha are obviously going to hunt all of the given prey types, its just a matter of what they as a group believe to be the most dangerous threat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any wolf would know how to pick off a weak, isolated deer, but a herd of healthy specimens is a different matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T09:49:44-07:00","id":101995,"title":"","content":"I'm relieved to see that &quot;chosen prey&quot; is a jumping-off point for re-focusing the Tribes rather than a central, all-consuming theme; my biggest complaint about the Tribes was how three of them could be summed up in a single word (warriors, alphas, mystics). For a moment, I was worried that my beloved Hunters-in-Darkness were going to go a similar way (described as only &quot;They hunt the hosts.&quot;). But they're not, so that's all right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","user":"Daydreamer","date":". 03-31-2014, 12:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T06:50:03-07:00","id":102603,"title":"","content":"I admit I actually like that the tribes might not be as culture based as before. While the tribes got a lot of good expanding in later books, and I love the Storm Lords mythos, I still felt the tribes were a bit strange in a pack based society.<br /> <br /> Now, they have a clear point aside from being a cultural group, and it is easy to see why and how an uratha joins a tribe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T07:02:15-07:00","id":102605,"title":"","content":"Not totally sold on this idea yet. I'll have to see more to make a final decision for myself.<br /> <br /> It does seem help firm up the Tribal identities.....but then I was one of the few who seemed to have a firm idea about them already.<br /> <br /> It does pull the Tribes away from being a little too close to the Auspices in their focus........but it could focus them a bit too much on one thing. I see the potential here for cross-Tribal conflict with regards to a single prey or territory. While full of dramatic potential, it could easily tear a pack apart. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;The spirits are the ones making this mess!&quot;<br /> &quot;No, it's the Pure stirring them up!&quot;<br /> &quot;Would you two shut up! It's clearly the humans helping them that's the <i>real </i>problem!&quot; </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T10:46:30-07:00","id":102775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/100915-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-houses-of-the-moon-tribes?p=102605#post102605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The spirits are the ones making this mess!&quot;<br /> &quot;No, it's the Pure stirring them up!&quot;<br /> &quot;Would you two shut up! It's clearly the humans helping them that's the <i>real </i>problem!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see this happening unless a pack is already naturally divisive. While each tribe has a different focus as to whom they believe is the best prey, they don't filter every problem through that lens. If a spirit is stirring up trouble, it would most likely be seen through an Auspice lens rather than a tribal.<br /> <br /> In the case above, it would be more of<br /> &quot;The spirits are making a mess!&quot;<br /> &quot;I vote we should beat it up!&quot;<br /> &quot;NO! Let us find out why it is making a mess first&quot;<br /> <br /> Something like that, but all would agree it is a spirit, that it was making a mess, and that they each have a different method to get rid of it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T11:27:53-07:00","id":102801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/100915-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-houses-of-the-moon-tribes?p=102775#post102775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see this happening unless a pack is already <b>naturally divisive</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um.....HELLO......WEREWOLVES!!!<br /> <br /> I'm kidding, you've got a valid point. Maybe I'm just used to people who play vampires too much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T20:46:14-07:00","id":103115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/100915-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-houses-of-the-moon-tribes?p=102801#post102801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um.....HELLO......WEREWOLVES!!!<br /> <br /> I'm kidding, you've got a valid point. Maybe I'm just used to people who play vampires too much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Knowing that you are joking, please take this following comment at full comedic value<br /> <br /> VAMPIRES ARE NOT WEREWOLVES!!!!<br /> <br /> With that out of the way,<br /> Werewolves are one of the best splats in the game to actually keep things in order assuming all the players are semi-decent roleplayers or able to play along if not. There is an established hierarchy within each pack and while an Alpha could rule as everything goes his way, they don't stay as Alpha for long by doing that. A wise Alpha will defer to the strengths of his pack to deal with an issue or at least solicit advice.<br /> <br /> So, again using your example of a spirit, if Alpha Fisty McPuncher the Blood Talon Rahu thinks the Pure are behind it, and refuses to accept another option, they may hunt down the spirit expecting the Pure only to run headlong into a Minor Incarna of which they were wholly unprepared for. What will follow is the pack Bone Shadow angrily telling him &quot;I told you so!&quot; followed by an immediate attempt to remove Fisty from his position of Alpha citing negligence and reckless endangerment to pack as a legitimate excuse.<br /> <br /> Fisty becomes Beta at best, or pack bitch at worst until he can redeem himself while the previous Beta on the totem pole gleefully walks over to Fisty's former prime sleeping spot and claims it for his own. Fisty now needs to sulk in the smallest of the rooms or the dampest of the sleeping spots all due to his recklessness and tunnel vision.<br /> <br /> God I love Werewolf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":444,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","user":"Dessembrae","date":". 03-31-2014, 11:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T22:19:41-07:00","id":103175,"title":"","content":"On the other hand, Werewolf is a game of extreme temperments, particularly angry ones. Just because it's not a game where the usual gains you'd find in Vampire come in often doesn't mean that a pack still won't frequently fight each other.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, these tend to be faster affairs, and <i>normally</i>more forgivable. But they don't have to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T23:14:16-07:00","id":103206,"title":"","content":"This whole thing implies that werewolves will suffer from tunnel vision regarding their favoured prey to begin with. I doubt it will be written like that in any way. Just because you favour a kind of prey does not mean you think that they are behind EVERYTHING EVER. A pack will likely quickly learn how to properly assess a situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T23:45:33-07:00","id":103226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/100915-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-houses-of-the-moon-tribes?p=103206#post103206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This whole thing implies that werewolves will suffer from tunnel vision regarding their favoured prey to begin with. I doubt it will be written like that in any way. Just because you favour a kind of prey does not mean you think that they are behind EVERYTHING EVER. A pack will likely quickly learn how to properly assess a situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although I can imagine a young pack falling into that thinking - &quot;Every virologists sees the problem as a virus&quot; and all","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T23:56:41-07:00","id":103232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/100915-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-houses-of-the-moon-tribes?p=103226#post103226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Although I can imagine a young pack falling into that thinking - &quot;Every virologists sees the problem as a virus&quot; and all</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they probably grow out of it quickly enough. Or die.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T00:04:28-07:00","id":103235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/100915-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-houses-of-the-moon-tribes?p=103232#post103232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, they probably grow out of it quickly enough. Or die.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having been rereading the corebook these last few weeks, I can confirm that that is indeed how pack formation works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T00:12:42-07:00","id":103241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/100915-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-houses-of-the-moon-tribes?p=103235#post103235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having been rereading the corebook these last few weeks, I can confirm that that is indeed how pack formation works.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what you're saying is that it's like college dorms.<br /> <br /> My surprise amounts to zero, but it's good to reflect on all the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T12:57:01-07:00","id":103593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/100915-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-houses-of-the-moon-tribes?p=103115#post103115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Knowing that you are joking, please take this following comment at full comedic value<br /> <br /> VAMPIRES ARE NOT WEREWOLVES!!!!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, duh......vampires are SOOOO much cooler. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> But, really, I should have phrased that better. Maybe I'm just used to players that get too myopic about their splats. I've seen too many WOD (new and classic) games go that way because of the (perceived) limitations of the groups in question......they just were usually playing vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 04-01-2014, 03:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T13:07:24-07:00","id":103608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/100915-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-houses-of-the-moon-tribes?p=103593#post103593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, really, I should have phrased that better. Maybe I'm just used to players that get too myopic about their splats. I've seen too many WOD (new and classic) games go that way because of the (perceived) limitations of the groups in question......they just were usually playing vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that method of thinking is a bit of a trap. Everyone wants to enjoy the game, and as such usually play splats with more perceived power behind them. Werewolves compared to other splats are fairly weak especially in a crossover setting especially when compared to Vampires. From my experience it usually comes down to people asking &quot;which is stronger?&quot; rather than &quot;what makes this splat fun to play?&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T14:33:59-07:00","id":103641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/100915-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-houses-of-the-moon-tribes?p=103608#post103608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that method of thinking is a bit of a trap. Everyone wants to enjoy the game, and as such usually play splats with more perceived power behind them. <i><b>Werewolves compared to other splats are fairly weak especially in a crossover setting especially when compared to Vampires</b></i>. From my experience it usually comes down to people asking &quot;which is stronger?&quot; rather than &quot;what makes this splat fun to play?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting take, since our table sees Werewolves as Far More Powerful than Vampires. Even in a Crossover. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Of course, I guess that depends... In games with more Vampires, I imagine it would possibly swing towards them. Most of our Crossovers in the last few years favored more Werewolves than Vampires. In the Previous Editions (oWOD), The Vampires Waffle-Stomped the Werewolf crossover characters, but then, it was primarily a Vampire Game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 04-01-2014, 05:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T14:52:51-07:00","id":103654,"title":"","content":"Seems to be all about what table you're sitting at. The one NWOD crossover I ran, the Mage and the Werewolf were competing for top slot, but that was more about the <i>player </i>of the Werewolf since he got <b>damn clever</b> with his powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T15:38:09-07:00","id":103677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/100915-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-houses-of-the-moon-tribes?p=103641#post103641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting take, since our table sees Werewolves as Far More Powerful than Vampires. Even in a Crossover. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Of course, I guess that depends... In games with more Vampires, I imagine it would possibly swing towards them. Most of our Crossovers in the last few years favored more Werewolves than Vampires. In the Previous Editions (oWOD), The Vampires Waffle-Stomped the Werewolf crossover characters, but then, it was primarily a Vampire Game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of the issue is that Werewolf powers are greatly geared towards more werewolves or versus spirits in particular. Vampire powers affect pretty much everyone and Obfuscate is one of the most powerful lines in the game especially since Werewolves have no method of piercing it. Vampires also have easier access to extreme forms of mind control powers which puts anything from the Werewolf Dominate list to shame.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems to be all about what table you're sitting at. The one NWOD crossover I ran, the Mage and the Werewolf were competing for top slot, but that was more about the <i>player </i>of the Werewolf since he got <b>damn clever</b> with his powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Proving once and for all that a good storyteller will reward creativity rather than throttle them at every attempt if it doesn't coincide EXACTLY to how the book describes it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T15:49:33-07:00","id":103685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/100915-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-houses-of-the-moon-tribes?p=103654#post103654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems to be all about what table you're sitting at. The one NWOD crossover I ran, the Mage and the Werewolf were competing for top slot, but that was more about the <i>player </i>of the Werewolf since he got <b>damn clever</b> with his powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>IME 90% of the time it's the players, not the splats, that are the deciding factor in crossover 'power'. But that can't be white-roomed, so people just bicker about Mages instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T17:23:13-07:00","id":103726,"title":"","content":"I can totally white room player cleverness, inthat I toss the two of them into a white room with an angry wolverine and whatever MacGuyver used in the last episode I watched.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T17:54:43-07:00","id":103734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/100915-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-houses-of-the-moon-tribes?p=103726#post103726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can totally white room player cleverness, inthat I toss the two of them into a white room with an angry wolverine and whatever MacGuyver used in the last episode I watched.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel that you missed a prime opportunity by using an angry wolverine. Instead, have you considered using a honey badger?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T18:15:26-07:00","id":103747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/100915-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-houses-of-the-moon-tribes?p=103734#post103734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel that you missed a prime opportunity by using an angry wolverine. Instead, have you considered using a honey badger?</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite frankly I use whatever ill-tempered animal I can find. I did this one thing with mutated sea bass, once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T22:50:39-07:00","id":103857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/100915-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-houses-of-the-moon-tribes?p=103734#post103734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel that you missed a prime opportunity by using an angry wolverine. Instead, have you considered using a honey badger?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not by chance from the Olympia, WA area, are you? My old college play group's mascot was the honey badger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T06:24:26-07:00","id":103992,"title":"","content":"Honey Badger don't care!!!!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T13:13:55-07:00","id":104289,"title":"","content":"White Room Scenarios may not be the titular idea behind game design. But when you go in thinking both splats are equal and one steamrolls over the other it tends to set a certain tone for how people perceive things. A brand new fan to the games wouldn't expect the splat about savage fury to have powers that rely on niche situations and conditions while a splat about investigations and solving mysteries to have powers about brute forcing things til they get their way. <br /> <br /> I love Werewolf. The fluff is just beautiful to me, but the crunch leaves me out in the cold damn near every time. I can see cleverness being rewarded, but sometimes you just want a power you built up to over long sessions to actually be something &quot;cool&quot;. And seeing how Werewolves are centered on the Shadow I'd rather they have more of a powerful standing in it then a Mage that shoved points into Spirit. Its like I expect Geist to go well with the Underworld and Changeling to do better with Arcadia. If this is the centerpiece of your entire worldview I'd hope you were better situated to deal with it than a guy that has it as just a part of his splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T01:30:34-07:00","id":125075,"title":"","content":"Ok, I loved the whole ideia of &quot;Wolf must Hunt&quot; and the most dangerous preys for each moon tribe, I just have one question, Who said in game that those are the most dangerous preys ?<br /> It's just a conclusion that everyone just get it, or someone realy said this to each werewolf when they make the tribal oath, it's something that already exist in Pangea time or just came to light pos-unification of forsaken tribes?<br /> ps: sorry for bad english, it's not my mother language","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1684-qu1nc45","name":"Qu1nc45","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T01:34:51-07:00","id":125077,"title":"","content":"I think it would come down to a personal decision. If I have a character who's a coroner, who first-changes while he opens up a corpse and spiders start to pour out of it, with several trying to get into his head, literally, I'm pretty sure the marking experience would lead him to the Hunters in Darkness, for example.<br /> <br /> It's less &quot;this is the most dangerous prey&quot; and more &quot;This is the most <b>worthy</b> prey&quot; - almost like a sport fused with spirituality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T01:57:49-07:00","id":125081,"title":"","content":"It's a matter of personal philosophy and conviction, most likely.<br /> <br /> An Incarna of poverty is wreaking havoc in the Flesh. What do you think is most important? Hunt down the spirit itself? Destroy the Beshilu who gnawed the hole in the wall between worlds that allowed the spirit to enter the Flesh? Deal with the humans who caused the spirit of poverty to come to being in the first place, and who, without being aware of it, still supply it with Essence day by day? Take out the Pure allies who use it as a lodge's totem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T02:27:50-07:00","id":125086,"title":"","content":"Who decided what was the most dangerous prey? The exact answer would be lost to time, but presumably the earliest members of the tribe chose and were endorsed by their Firstborn totem, or the Firstborn told them what it expected and they complied. These days, it simple is - if you join that tribe, they teach you how best to hunt that sacred prey, and the Firstborn empowers it.<br /> <br /> Sacred prey isn't the only decider for joining a tribe, though. The tribes have other philosophies and values that attract members beyond what they hunt best. An Uratha who embraces change and adapting to it would drift towards the Iron Masters, even if they think spirits are the most dangerous thing. They'll soon be shown by the tribe how humans are more dangerous, but whether they fully accept this is up to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 05-04-2014, 08:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T03:59:21-07:00","id":125107,"title":"","content":"Subtopic in accord ( or Accord <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) with new Tribes. I need the ex-Bale Hound she-wolf that will be mentor figure for PCs and she choose people of small town she thinks are Wolf-Blooded to awoke the Wolf in them ( the PCs <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />). She want them to confront to seven Bale Hounds active in region and want's to make new Uratha in to pack that will finally destroy cultists. What would best fitting new Tribe take on this? She want's to fight werewolves now - obviously - but before she could be part of any other Tribe, yes? Whitch one would be most suitiable? And with that - what Auspice would you give her?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/ava